From 0ff456948ad64936fb089a0e6a3e163872d8c4e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:05:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/34] WP19: Readable guest links

Integration with WP18 (numbered migrations): the apartment_slug table and its partial unique index moved from db.SCHEMA into App/app/migrations/0002_apartment_slug.sql (CREATE ... IF NOT EXISTS), as AGENTS.md now requires; init_db runs guest_slug.backfill(conn) after apply_migrations. tests/test_migrations.py now runs on a copy of the shipped migration files and numbers its demo files after the latest one, so it keeps working as files are added. host_i18n.py: kept WP17's removal of apartment.form.guest_link.lede (the form uses guest_links.lede) and added WP19's name_label and name_hint in EN and CS. retention._delete_workspace keeps WP19's explicit apartment_slug delete, with WP18's plain = comparison. Test fix: tests/test_guest_slugs.py cleanup also removes the test owner's apartments, because the regenerate-link test replaces permalink_token and the leftover apartment made test_demo_seed fail when run after it (this also failed on the WP19 branch alone).

Query budget (WP14): onboarding reads the current slug in its apartment query, so the finished onboarding panel does not add a per-page apartment_slug query; this kept /reservations under the 20-query budget in tests/test_query_budget.py.

Conflict resolution: routes/guest.py import list: WP19's guest_slug added to WP26's list (WP26 already dropped host_i18n there). _components.html: the onboarding finish card keeps WP28's show_toggle switch and links the preview to WP19's finish.link_key. tests/test_guest_browser_e2e.py: WP19's shared _register_a_group_of_three helper now takes the guest language, so WP26's en/de/es/fr runs (no ?lang= for de/es/fr, privacy-page check) and WP19's readable-link runs share it on main's arrival-lane flow.
